T Jazz Snow K'NEX tilt rig v2
# U = 37.5 mm, z up, desk at z = 0. The frame stands on legs over the mouse, which sits at the origin.
# Push the bed with your fingers at the four F lines; the two fork rods carry the tilt down to the collar.
X mouse 0,0,0.507 62,117,38 #3B4252 mass=85 pad=1.5,0
! base frame, 6U square at z = 1.5U so the mouse clears it
C K1 W8 -3,-3,1.5
C K2 W8 3,-3,1.5
C K3 W8 3,3,1.5
C K4 W8 -3,3,1.5
C A1 W8 -2,-3,1.5
C A2 W8 2,-3,1.5
C A3 W8 2,3,1.5
C A4 W8 -2,3,1.5
C B1 W8 -3,-2,1.5
C B2 W8 3,-2,1.5
C B3 W8 3,2,1.5
C B4 W8 -3,2,1.5
R K1 A1
R A1 A2
R A2 K2
R K4 A4
R A4 A3
R A3 K3
R K1 B1
R B1 B4
R B4 K4
R K2 B2
R B2 B3
R B3 K3
R A1 B1
R A2 B2
R A3 B3
R A4 B4
! cross rails in the vertical planes x = +-2, hung off the frame by hidden greens
C F1 W8 -2,-2,1.5 x y
C F2 W8 2,-2,1.5 x y
C F3 W8 2,2,1.5 x y
C F4 W8 -2,2,1.5 x y
C RL W8 -2,0,1.5 x y
C RR W8 2,0,1.5 x y
R A1 F1
R A2 F2
R A3 F3
R A4 F4
! legs and feet: the feet are the only parts that touch the desk
C G1 W8 -2,-2,0.5 x y
C G2 W8 2,-2,0.5 x y
C G3 W8 2,2,0.5 x y
C G4 W8 -2,2,0.5 x y
C GL W8 -2,0,0.5 x y
C GR W8 2,0,0.5 x y
R F1 G1
R F2 G2
R F3 G3
R F4 G4
R RL GL
R RR GR
R G1 GL
R GL G4
R G2 GR
R GR G3
! towers: one unit tall over the rails, braced by white diagonals off split rails
C SL W8 -2,-1,1.5 x y
C NL W8 -2,1,1.5 x y
C SR W8 2,-1,1.5 x y
C NR W8 2,1,1.5 x y
R F1 SL
R SL RL
R RL NL
R NL F4
R F2 SR
R SR RR
R RR NR
R NR F3
C TL W8 -2,0,2.5 x y
C TR W8 2,0,2.5 x y
R RL TL
R RR TR
R SL TL
R NL TL
R SR TR
R NR TR
! pitch axle: a grey rod capped at both ends, riding in the two tower hubs; spacers stop it wandering
R -2.828,0,2.5 2.828,0,2.5 grey
C CL D1 -2.828,0,2.5 y x
C CR D1 2.828,0,2.5 y -x
P -2.2,0,2.5 silver
P -1.8,0,2.5 silver
P 1.8,0,2.5 silver
P 2.2,0,2.5 silver
! ring: two hubs on the pitch axle, white V up to a rectangle at z = 4.5U carrying the roll bearings
H HL W8 -1,0,2.5 z
H HR W8 1,0,2.5 z
P -1.2,0,2.5 silver
P -0.8,0,2.5 silver
P 0.8,0,2.5 silver
P 1.2,0,2.5 silver
C JL1 W8 -1,-1,3.5 x y
C JL2 W8 -1,1,3.5 x y
C JR1 W8 1,-1,3.5 x y
C JR2 W8 1,1,3.5 x y
R HL JL1
R HL JL2
R HR JR1
R HR JR2
R JL1 JL2
R JR1 JR2
C QL1 W8 -1,-2,3.5
C QL2 W8 -1,2,3.5
C QR1 W8 1,-2,3.5
C QR2 W8 1,2,3.5
R JL1 QL1
R JL2 QL2
R JR1 QR1
R JR2 QR2
C FB W8 0,-2,3.5
C FF W8 0,2,3.5
R QL1 FB
R FB QR1
R QL2 FF
R FF QR2
! roll axle: red rod end-on in the ring, carrying the bed's two hubs
R FB FF
! bed: two hubs on the roll axle, a flat deck one unit above on two 3D pairs
H BL W8 0,-1,3.5 z
H BR W8 0,1,3.5 z
P 0,-1.2,3.5 silver
P 0,-0.8,3.5 silver
P 0,0.8,3.5 silver
P 0,1.2,3.5 silver
C DL B7 0,-1,4.5 x z
C DL2 B7 0,-1,4.5 z x
C DR B7 0,1,4.5 x z
C DR2 B7 0,1,4.5 z x
R BL DL
R BR DR
C SM W8 0,0,4.5
C PL W8 -1,0,4.5
C PR W8 1,0,4.5
C N1 W8 -1,-1,4.5
C N2 W8 1,-1,4.5
C N3 W8 1,1,4.5
C N4 W8 -1,1,4.5
R SM DL2
R SM DR2
R SM PL
R SM PR
R DL2 N1
R DL2 N2
R DR2 N3
R DR2 N4
R PL N1
R PL N4
R PR N2
R PR N3
R SM N1
R SM N2
R SM N3
R SM N4
! deck edges and the two arms that reach past the frame to carry the forks
C DB W8 0,-2,4.5
C DF W8 0,2,4.5
C SL1 W8 -1,-2,4.5
C SR1 W8 1,-2,4.5
C SL2 W8 -1,2,4.5
C SR2 W8 1,2,4.5
R DL2 DB
R DR2 DF
R N1 SL1
R N2 SR1
R N3 SR2
R N4 SL2
R DB SL1
R DB SR1
R DF SL2
R DF SR2
C TB W8 0,-3,4.5
C TF W8 0,3,4.5
R DB TB
R DF TF
R TB SL1
R TB SR1
R TF SL2
R TF SR2
C HB W8 0,-4,4.5 x z
C HF W8 0,4,4.5 x z
R TB HB
R TF HF
! centring springs: four red rods anchored in the frame, sliding through hubs in the deck.
! They are the only thing holding the bed level; the sim shows the rig flops without them.
C UL1 W8 -2,-1,4.5
C UL2 W8 -2,1,4.5
C UR1 W8 2,-1,4.5
C UR2 W8 2,1,4.5
R N1 UL1
R N4 UL2
R N2 UR1
R N3 UR2
R SL -2,-1,5.5 red beam
R NL -2,1,5.5 red beam
R SR 2,-1,5.5 red beam
R NR 2,1,5.5 red beam
! fork: two red rods bending under the deck arms, rigid into the collar so it hangs at the mouse's waist
R HB 0,-4,0.5 red beam
R HF 0,4,0.5 red beam
! collar: hangs at 18.75 mm, the mouse's mid height, and pushes it in x and y
C XB R3 0,-4,0.5 -x z
C XF R3 0,4,0.5 x z
C EB W8 0,-3,0.5
C EF W8 0,3,0.5
R XB EB
R XF EF
C ML1 G4 -1,-2,0.5 z x-y
C MR1 G4 1,-2,0.5 z y
C ML2 G4 -1,2,0.5 z -y
C MR2 G4 1,2,0.5 z -x+y
C CLm O2 -1,0,0.5 z y
C CRm O2 1,0,0.5 z y
R EB ML1
R EB MR1
R EF ML2
R EF MR2
R ML1 CLm
R CLm ML2
R MR1 CRm
R CRm MR2
R ML1 MR1
R ML2 MR2
! fingers: press a bed pad to tilt. 3 N is a light press, 8 N is firm.
F DF 0,0,-3 finger front
F DB 0,0,-3 finger back
F PL 0,0,-3 finger left
F PR 0,0,-3 finger right
